Architecture Overview • Development Guide
📌 Executive Summary

CHRONOS (Closed-loop Hybrid Reservoir Optimization and Navigation Operating System) is an enterprise-grade autonomous control platform engineered for continuous optimization of naturally flowing oil wells. Operating oil production wells requires balancing crude oil extraction rate against rigid physical constraints—such as Wellhead Pressure ( W H P ), Flowline Pressure ( F L P ), and Bottomhole Pressure ( B H P ). Manual or heuristic valve adjustments often result in constraint overshoot, production loss, or severe reservoir instability.

CHRONOS addresses this challenge through a closed-loop Receding-Horizon Model Predictive Control (MPC) architecture coupled with First-Order Plus Dead Time (FOPDT) dynamic system identification. By dynamically evaluating state trajectories over a rolling prediction horizon ( H = 3  hours ) and embedding a robust 3 safety back-off margin, CHRONOS guarantees safe operating limit compliance while maximizing oil throughput.
✨ Key Capabilities & Features

    ⚙️ FOPDT Dynamic Model Identification: Automated parameter estimation ( K , τ , b ) using non-linear least-squares optimization (scipy.optimize.curve_fit) derived from open-loop step-test data.
    🎯 Receding-Horizon MPC Engine: Fast, candidate-evaluating predictive optimizer that balances target tracking against choke move penalties to prevent valve chattering.
    🛡️ Robust Safety Back-Off Margin: Built-in 3 constraint tightening on upper and lower bounds ( W H P , F L P , B H P ) to guarantee safety under model-plant mismatch and process noise.
    🔄 Autonomous Saturation Management: Intelligent handling of unreachable oil rate targets (Scenario C) by safely saturating production at the maximum feasible envelope limit without boundary violations.
    📊 Comprehensive Analytics & Diagnostics: Integrated plotting and metrics reporting suite evaluating Mean Absolute Error ( MAE ), Root Mean Square Error ( RMSE ), and constraint violation counts.

📐 System Architecture

CHRONOS seamlessly integrates high-fidelity physical simulation, dynamic data identification, and closed-loop predictive control:
🛢️ Physical System & Governing Dynamics
1. State Variables & Physical Quantities

The well state vector x ( t ) ∈ R 4 and control input u ( t ) ∈ R 1 are defined as:

    u ( t ) : Choke Valve Opening Percentage () ∈ [ 0 , 100 ]
    Q ( t ) : Crude Oil Production Rate ( bbl/hr )
    W H P ( t ) : Wellhead Pressure ( psi )
    F L P ( t ) : Flowline Pressure ( psi )
    B H P ( t ) : Bottomhole Pressure ( psi )

2. Discrete FOPDT State Equation

For each state variable y ∈ Q , W H P , F L P , B H P , dynamic progression over interval Δ t = 1.0  hr is governed by:

y [ k + 1 ] = y [ k ] + Δ t τ y ( K y ⋅ u [ k ] + b y − y [ k ] )

Where K y represents the static gain, τ y is the time constant (hours), and b y is the baseline intercept.
