EATS-RTOS: Energy-Adaptive Task Scheduling for FreeRTOS on ESP32

EATS-RTOS Banner

FreeRTOS ESP32 Language License Energy Reduction Emergency Latency

A cross-layer, protocol-aware power management framework for IoT endpoints running FreeRTOS on ESP32 dual-core microcontrollers.

Key Features • Architecture • Benchmarks • Quick Start • Repository Structure
📌 Problem Statement & Solution Overview

Embedded IoT devices operate under severe energy constraints: radio-frequency communication (WiFi, BLE) requires peak CPU throughput, yet inter-transmission idle intervals constitute over 78% of device operating lifetime.

Standard FreeRTOS deployments on ESP32 hold the CPU clock frequency statically at 240 MHz, dissipating 160–200 mA even while waiting on basic timer interrupts.

Baseline (Static 240 MHz):  [   180 mA Idle   ][ 320 mA WiFi ][   180 mA Idle   ] (High Power Floor)
EATS-RTOS (Adaptive DVFS):  [ 30 mA (40MHz)   ][ 264mA WiFi  ][ 30 mA (40MHz)   ] (~81.4% Energy Savings)

EATS-RTOS solves this energy waste by:

    Dynamic Voltage & Frequency Scaling (DVFS/DFS): Automatically scaling CPU frequency between 40 , MHz (Idle), 80 , MHz (BLE), and 240 , MHz (WiFi).
    Workload-Sensitive Priority Weighting: Computing priority boost factors dynamically from transmission payload length and duration.
    Core-Affinity Partitioning: Isolating WiFi/BLE stacks on Core 0 while real-time sensor processing runs on Core 1.
    Hard Real-Time Emergency Guarantees: Implementing an emergency ceiling override providing sub-5ms alarm latency.

✨ Key Features

    ⚡ Protocol-Aware DVFS Engine: Seamless clock scaling down to 40 MHz idle setpoint ( 76.3 drop in idle current draw).
    🧮 Workload-Sensitive Dynamic Priority: Priority function π i ( t ) = π base ( i ) + w ( protocol , workload ) with logarithmic payload scaling.
    🛡️ Priority Inversion Protection: Mutex priority inheritance (configUSE_MUTEXES = 1) preventing unbounded task blocking.
    🚨 Fast-Path Emergency Override: Priority 20 ceiling override for emergency flame sensors, bypassing supervisory loop delay.
    ⏱️ Negligible DVFS Overhead: Bounded 12 , μ s switching cost ( 0.0006 overhead relative to management period).
    📊 Automated Plotting & Metrics: Integrated Python data analytics suite generating publication-quality graphs.

