VISOR
Visual-Inertial Scene Observation & Reconstruction

C++ Standard OpenCV Intel RealSense OpenMP License

High-performance C++17 real-time 3D TSDF volumetric scene reconstruction engine powered by Intel RealSense D455 depth hardware and IMU sensor fusion.

Key Features • Architecture • Prerequisites • Quick Start • Interactive Controls • Documentation
📌 Project Overview

VISOR (Visual-Inertial Scene Observation & Reconstruction) is an optimized 3D scanning and scene reconstruction framework designed for autonomous robotics, rover navigation, and high-fidelity 3D spatial mapping.

By coupling Intel RealSense D455 depth hardware, Intel-optimized spatial/temporal noise filters, OpenCV KinFu (Kinect Fusion), and a Complementary IMU Filter, VISOR provides dense, low-drift 3D point cloud generation in real time.
⚡ Key Features
Feature 	Standard KinFu (kinfu.cpp) 	IMU-Enhanced KinFu (enhanced_kinfu.cpp)
Depth Sensor Stream 	848x480 @ 30 FPS 	848x480 @ 30 FPS
Intel Post-Processing Chain 	Decimation, Spatial, Temporal, Hole Fill 	Decimation, Spatial, Temporal, Hole Fill
IMU Sensor Fusion 	❌ 	✅ (Accel + Gyro Complementary Filter)
Adaptive Distance Clipping 	Static (0.2m - 1.5m) 	Dynamic (1.2m Active / 1.5m Static)
Tracking Loss Recovery 	Immediate Reset 	5-Frame Motion Stability Buffer
HUD Telemetry Overlay 	Minimal Controls 	Pitch, Roll, Motion & Tracking Status
3D Point Cloud Export 	ASCII .ply 	ASCII .ply
📐 System Architecture

The VISOR pipeline continuously acquires depth frames and motion vectors from the Intel RealSense D455, processes them through an edge-preserving filter chain and an IMU fusion filter, and feeds the resulting frames into a TSDF (Truncated Signed Distance Function) volumetric grid.
