AprilTag TurtleBot Alignment (ROS 2)

A ROS 2 package for real-time AprilTag visual marker tracking and autonomous robot alignment. It captures video from a webcam, detects AprilTags using OpenCV and the apriltag Python library, and publishes velocity commands (cmd_vel) to steer and align a mobile robot (e.g., TurtleBot).
🚀 Features

    Real-Time Visual Tracking: Captures live camera feeds (10 Hz) and detects AprilTag markers.
    Visual Annotations: Renders bounding boxes, center coordinates, relative pixel displacements, and estimated size overlays.
    Autonomous Alignment Control:
        Angular Control (Steering): Rotates left or right when the tag is off-center (|x| > 50px).
        Linear Control (Distance): Moves forward or backward based on perceived tag pixel size (> 350px or < 250px).
    ROS 2 Integration: Publishes standard geometry_msgs/msg/Twist messages to /cmd_vel.

🛠️ Prerequisites & Dependencies

Before running this package, ensure you have ROS 2 installed along with the following Python dependencies:

    ROS 2 (Humble, Iron, or newer)
    Python 3
    OpenCV: pip install opencv-python
    NumPy: pip install numpy
    AprilTag: pip install apriltag

Ensure a compatible USB webcam or camera is connected to /dev/video0.
